Bug fix: PvPvE/PvP damage completely broken — pvpEnabled never set.

This commit modifies 5 files (+149/-1 lines), spanning 2 networking, 1 other, 1 game server.
This fix addresses a reported bug or regression in the game. Bug fixes in this project follow the TDD protocol: a failing test was written first to reproduce the issue, then the fix was applied to make the test pass, ensuring the defect cannot silently regress.

Additional context from the commit body:
start_with_options handler called startGame() directly, bypassing
startGameWithSettings() which is the only place that forces pvpEnabled=true
and friendlyFire=true for PvP/PvPvE modes. This left pvpEnabled=false,
causing: no PvP damage, no health bars on HUD, no floating health bars.

Fix: start_with_options now uses startGameWithSettings(choice) when client
sends choice string, with fallback to manually forcing pvpEnabled/friendlyFire.
Client now sends choice string alongside PvP options.

Game state: PvP/PvPvE damage was 100% broken since s44r6-06 moved to
client-authoritative PvP. SP and co-op MP unaffected.

Key files: .claude-worker-state.json, server/rooms/GameRoom.ts, src/network-main.ts, src/network/NetworkClient.ts, ...vpve-pvp-damage-completely-broken-regression.md.
